+# Road to generated-artifact conflict drawdown — the repository-local cut
+
+> **Source:** maintainer handover 2026-08-21 (*"viele der Konflikte kommen durch
+> automatisch generierte Dateien … brauchen wir die zur Laufzeit? Oder für das
+> Repo? Die Dokumentation? Oder nur für die CI?"*), plus a 50-session transcript
+> measurement, plus a live re-measurement of every conflicting PR, plus an AI
+> council pass (2 seats + blind peer review, $0.12, 2026-08-21) recorded at
+> § Council verdict. Every number below was measured on `origin/main` at
+> `c00df51c6`. Nothing is carried from memory.
+
+## Goal
+
+The single path behind the largest share of this repository's merge conflicts —
+`agents/roadmaps-progress.md` — is no longer tracked, and its freshness gate
+tells tracked and untracked apart **explicitly** rather than by inferring intent
+from a missing file. The second-largest **authored** conflict surface, the
+appending stubs index, stops appending. Two further generated paths the conflict
+tool still routes to a human decision are classified. Everything the council
+refused to greenlight — the consumer rollout, the estate-budget history split,
+the gate-baseline split — is carried with its named blocker rather than shipped
+half-analysed.
+
+## § 0 Findings
+
+**F1 — 90 % of conflict occurrences are on generated files, and the population
+is four paths wide.** Across the 50 most recent session transcripts, **28 of 50
+sessions (56 %)** hit at least one merge conflict; 113 conflict records name 16
+distinct paths, of which **89.9 % of occurrences** are on generated or
+baseline files and only three paths are genuinely authored. Independently,
+`git merge-tree --write-tree origin/main origin/<branch>` over **all three** PRs
+GitHub reports `CONFLICTING` (#1505, #1504, #1495) returns *exactly the same
+four paths and nothing else*:
+
+| Path | class | 60-day commits | sessions hit | consumed by |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `agents/roadmaps-progress.md` | generated dashboard | **830** | **20** | nothing in this repo's CI |
+| `agents/roadmaps/stubs/README.md` | **authored** prose index, no generator | — | 2 | prose only |
+| `src/config/estate-count-budget.json` | ratchet baseline | 93 | 11 | `check_estate_count.ts` |
+| `src/config/gate-violation-baselines.json` | ratchet baseline | 55 | 3 | ~20 gates via `gate_baseline.ts:42` |
+
+**F2 — the maintainer's question, answered per class.** The handover asks whether
+these artefacts are needed at runtime, in the repo, in the docs, or only in CI.
+Measured, not assumed:
+
+| Artefact | tracked? | why |
+|---|---|---|
+| `.claude/`, `.augment/`, `.cursor/`, `.clinerules/`, `.windsurfrules` | **already untracked** — 0 tracked files each | regenerated by `task generate-tools`; nothing to do |
+| `dist/agent-src/` (1170 files), `dist/router.json`, `dist/install/`, `.claude-plugin/`, `src/config/` | **must stay** | shipped to npm via `package.json` `files[]`; a consumer install reads them |
+| `docs/proof.md`, `docs/CLAIMS.md`, `docs/catalog.md` | stay | published by `deploy-site.yml`, which triggers on those exact paths |
+| `docs/decisions/INDEX.md` | stays | many inbound doc links; generated, but a docs surface |
+| `agents/roadmaps/archive/{INDEX.md,index.json}` | stay | read on disk by `archive_completed_roadmaps.ts` and `ship_diff_volume_hook.ts`; already paired-`--check`ed; **0/3** live conflicts |
+| **`agents/roadmaps-progress.md`** | **no** | **zero** references under `.github/workflows/`; one `taskfiles/content.yml` target; one real inbound link. A local convenience view — the maintainer's own reading, confirmed by measurement |
+| `src/config/*-budget.json` ratchets | must stay | the committed number *is* the mechanism (ADR-239) |
+
+**F3 — the repo-side blocker is one comparison, and it reproduces.**
+`update_roadmap_progress.ts:1337` sets `current = fs.existsSync(target) ? read : ''`
+and `:1360` sets `stale = current !== new_text`, so an absent file is
+indistinguishable from a stale one. Probed in a scratch worktree on `c00df51c6`,
+failing direction first: with the file present `--check` exits **0**
+(`✅ … is up to date`); with the file deleted it exits **1**
+(`❌ agents/roadmaps-progress.md is stale`). The tree was restored from a `cp`
+backup and verified clean (`git status --porcelain` empty, 312 lines back).
+
+**F4 — the generator's self-header makes a claim untracking falsifies.**
+`:1002` writes *"(timestamp lives in git history)"*. Once the file is untracked
+there is no git history for it, so the header would assert something false about
+its own provenance.
+
+**F5 — the stubs index has no generator.** 133 lines of hand-written prose,
+**zero** `- [` list items; every roadmap-transfer session appends a section by
+hand. There is nothing to regenerate — the conflict is authored churn on an
+index whose content is derivable from the directory listing beside it.
+
+**F6 — two generated paths are still routed to a human decision.** The 50-session
+measurement found `docs/decisions/INDEX.md` in **4 distinct sessions** and
+`dist/router.json` in 1. Neither is matched by `sync_pr_branch.ts`'s `GENERATED`
+list: the first is written by `src/scripts/adr/regenerate_index.ts` with a
+dynamic directory argument (so the literal never appears in a grep and was
+missed), and the second sits under `dist/` while the list carries only the
+`dist/agent-src/` prefix. Both have exactly one correct resolution —
+regenerate — and the tool currently says "make a human decision", which is the
+same defect the list's own comment already records once for
+`src/scripts/hook_manifest.json`.
